# The desktop app generates a random local dashboard token at runtime.
# Provider keys are written through Hermes' authenticated /api/env endpoint.

# Demo fixtures are HARD-DISABLED in production. `?demo=1` is honored only in a
# dev server or an explicit QA/test build. To produce a QA build that can drive
# the installed demo-transport e2e, use `npm run build:qa` / `package:win:qa`.
# The QA flag is derived from the Vite build mode in vite.config.ts
# (`--mode qa` sets VITE_ALLOW_DEMO=true); there is no `.env.qa` file to edit.
# A shipping production build bakes nothing, so demo fixtures are absent.
